          <!-- ───────────────────────────────────────── [09] Automations -->
          <section class="auto" id="automations" aria-labelledby="auto-title">
            <div class="head">
              <div class="head__main">
                <p class="tag">[09] Automations</p>
                <h2 id="auto-title" class="h2" data-reveal>Agents that start themselves.</h2>
              </div>
              <p class="body head__aside" data-reveal>
                Run a task every morning, or whenever GitHub opens a pull request. An agent can watch its
                pull request and wake when checks finish or someone comments.
              </p>
            </div>
            <!-- One weekday, three ways an agent starts without you. Each row names the trigger and draws
                 its run on the shared day: the trigger's mark, the agent at work, done. Times are
                 fractions of the day (--x starts, --y ends, --w the pull request's wake), and each mark
                 draws in as the playhead passes it (drafting.js sets --p; see [05]). -->
            <figure class="day" data-day>
              <ol class="day__rows">
                <li class="day__row">
                  <div class="day__label">
                    <h3 class="day__title">On a schedule</h3>
                    <p class="day__note">Every few hours, or at a set time on the days you choose.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="day__lane" style="--x: 0.2917; --y: 0.3958" aria-hidden="true">
                    <span class="day__trig k-fade">Weekdays 07:00</span>
                    <i class="day__run k-grow"></i>
                    <i class="day__dot day__dot--start k-fade"></i>
                    <i class="day__dot day__dot--end k-fade"></i>
                    <span class="day__done k-fade">Done</span>
                    <span class="day__task k-fade">Claude · triages new issues</span>
                  </div>
                </li>
                <li class="day__row">
                  <div class="day__label">
                    <h3 class="day__title">On a webhook</h3>
                    <p class="day__note">GitHub opens a pull request and an agent starts on it. Signed requests only.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="day__lane" style="--x: 0.4861; --y: 0.5764" aria-hidden="true">
                    <span class="day__trig k-fade">GitHub opened #214</span>
                    <i class="day__run k-grow"></i>
                    <i class="day__dot day__dot--start k-fade"></i>
                    <i class="day__dot day__dot--end k-fade"></i>
                    <span class="day__done k-fade">Done</span>
                    <span class="day__task k-fade">Codex · reviews #214</span>
                  </div>
                </li>
                <li class="day__row">
                  <div class="day__label">
                    <h3 class="day__title">On its pull request</h3>
                    <p class="day__note">An agent waits on its pull request and wakes when checks finish or someone comments.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="day__lane day__lane--wake" style="--x: 0; --w: 0.6389; --y: 0.7361" aria-hidden="true">
                    <span class="day__trig k-fade">Waiting on #212</span>
                    <i class="day__wait k-grow"></i>
                    <i class="day__run k-grow"></i>
                    <i class="day__dot day__dot--start k-fade"></i>
                    <i class="day__dot day__dot--fail k-fade"></i>
                    <span class="day__fail k-fade">Checks failed 15:20</span>
                    <i class="day__dot day__dot--end k-fade"></i>
                    <span class="day__done k-fade">Done</span>
                    <span class="day__task k-fade">Claude · fixes the test</span>
                  </div>
                </li>
              </ol>
              <div class="day__axis" aria-hidden="true">
                <span style="--x: 0">00:00</span>
                <span style="--x: 0.25">06:00</span>
                <span style="--x: 0.5">12:00</span>
                <span style="--x: 0.75">18:00</span>
                <span style="--x: 1">24:00</span>
              </div>
              <div class="day__head" aria-hidden="true"><i><span data-day-time>00:00</span></i></div>
              <figcaption class="day__cap">
                <span class="tag" aria-hidden="true">Fig. 3 · One weekday</span>
                <span class="sr-only">One weekday of automations. At 07:00 a schedule starts Claude on the night’s new issues, and it finishes by 09:30. At 11:40 GitHub opens pull request 214, and a webhook starts Codex on a review. Claude has been waiting on pull request 212 since the day began; its checks fail at 15:20, Claude wakes and fixes the test, and is done by 17:40.</span>
              </figcaption>
            </figure>
          </section>
